+# Filtering the Veterinarian Directory Is Not Search
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable entity. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey. Its provenance stayed open: nobody had said whether it was deliberately declined.
+
+A request on 2026-09-13 asked to narrow the veterinarian directory to one specialty. Read literally, NG-9 covered that request, because narrowing a list of veterinarians resembles searching for one. The owner decided the row at intake:
+
+> Non-goal NG-9 is narrowed: free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Hold NG-9 as written.** Any narrowing of the directory stays out. Rejected by the owner decision above.
+2. **Drop NG-9's veterinarian clause.** Veterinarian search of every kind opens. Rejected: the owner keeps free-text veterinarian search out of scope.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Free-text veterinarian search stays declined. Filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is not search, so the row no longer covers it.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 no longer excludes filtering the veterinarian directory by an attribute the directory already shows. Free-text search for a veterinarian stays out of scope. The owner stated no new reason, so the row's existing rationale is left unchanged.
+
+The decision covers the veterinarian clause only. The owner did not address the pet and visit clauses, so their provenance stays open with the rest of the table.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The directory may be narrowed to one specialty. `REQ-VET-003` records that capability.
+- A later request to filter by another attribute the directory shows needs no NG-9 change. Where such a filter ends and free-text search begins is an open question in the PRD.
+- A request for free-text veterinarian search still meets NG-9 and proceeds only on a recorded owner decision.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and the updated preamble.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the capability the narrowing admits.
