+# Reads Keyed by Caller-Supplied Text Stay Out of the Cache
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+The vet cache holds the two unfiltered veterinarian reads. Its configuration sets no size limit and no expiry, and nothing evicts from it.
+
+`REQ-VET-003` adds a read keyed by a specialty name the caller types into the address. If that read were cached, every distinct name any caller sent would add an entry that is never removed. Memory would then grow without bound, driven entirely from outside.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Cache the narrowed read in the existing cache.** This is the simplest option, but it opens the unbounded growth described above.
+2. **Bound the cache.** Set a size limit or an expiry through the cache provider. That changes behavior for the unfiltered reads too, and the limit is provider-specific configuration the project does not carry today.
+3. **Cache only names that exist.** Resolve the name against the specialty list first, and cache only a hit. That bounds the keys, at the cost of a second lookup and a second rule.
+4. **Leave the narrowed read uncached** (chosen). The read goes to the database on every request.
+
+## Decision
+
+A read whose key includes caller-supplied text is not cached. The narrowed directory read carries no cache annotation. The unfiltered reads stay cached as before.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Caller input cannot grow memory through the cache.
+- Every narrowed request costs one query. For a directory of this size, that cost is negligible.
+- A later read keyed by caller text follows the same rule. That includes filtering by another attribute the directory shows, which the NG-9 narrowing admits. Revisiting it means bounding the cache first (option 2 or 3).
+- The unfiltered paged read's key already includes a caller-chosen page number. That exposure predates this decision and is not changed by it.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003
+
+- `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/vet/VetRepository.java`: the uncached narrowed read.
+- `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/system/CacheConfiguration.java`: the unbounded vet cache, unchanged.
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md § Contracts](../system-design.md#contracts) — the `VetRepository` row
+- [system-design.md § Threat Model](../system-design.md#threat-model)
